  "title": "ASUS Dial on Linux",
  "date": "2026-04-25T21:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "ASUS Dial on Linux\n\nOne reason I bought ASUS StudioBook Pro 16 is that it has a dial. And it was my major reason to stick on Windows. However, recently I turned to Linux and I found openwheel which is an open source driver for ASUS dial.\n\nIt has no system daemon for it to run at startup. so I added these two systemd services to run it at startup.\n\nThere are some occasions that the wheel services run failed because there is no graphical sessions. Make sure it runs after graphical-session\n\nGive them udev permissions, edit /etc/udev/rules.d/99-asus-wheel.rules\n\nApply the rules with:\n\nEnable them with:",
